### Resolution, 21 November 2026

The user confirmed satisfaction with the three findings, their wording and placement, and the interval treatment, and authorised closing Issue 05.

- **H2.** For 820 selected signings with enough scored sentences on both sides of the move, the main RoBERTa estimate was +0.0060 score points (30+ minus under-30 difference in changes, p = 0.7558). The analysis found no clear age difference in change, and smaller differences remain plausible. Omit the historical draft interval because its endpoints are saved but its construction is unverified. The separately traceable estimate-centred shuffle range and approximate detectable gap (0.0567) remain in the evidence inventory.
- **Exploratory H2b.** In the 793-signing all-controls comparison, the adjusted RoBERTa gap was −0.0349 after signing (p = 0.0390) and −0.0153 before (p = 0.3511). The before comparison provides context. The direct comparison of changes leaves uncertainty about a widening gap. The strength of the exploratory evidence depends on the specification, including market value. The saved wording explains why the analysis was run and how the regression compares signings. [Issue 15](2026-11-21_15-45-35_15-explain-h2b-model-and-figure.scratch) remains open for the worked model explanation, candidate figure and decision on retaining H2b in the paper.
- **Coverage volume.** Briefly report higher raw median Guardian article counts for older signings in both periods in Results. The 1,332 selected signings include those with zero articles. Discussion develops how more attention can coexist with lower tone scores. Keep the modelled ratio definitions and specifications in the evidence inventory.

These decisions preserve the exact Issue 02 sample description and the complete Issue 03 H1 passages. The Guardian and H1 event populations are separate. Issue 04's qualified measurement conclusion and older-player validation limitation still apply. No new analysis or script rerun was performed. The [approved evidence and wording](../evidence_and_sources.md#issue-05-guardian-tone-and-coverage-findings-21-november-2026), [storyline](../paper_storyline.md#proposed-guardian-results-and-discussion-21-november-2026), [research question notes](../final_research_question.md), [tracker](README.md), [repository context](REPOSITORY_CONTEXT.md) and [README checkpoint](../README.md#current-checkpoint) record the outcome. Next is the [Issue 06 continuation prompt](2026-11-19_15-30-34_06-choose-network-analysis-role.scratch#continuation-prompt), starting with what H1 already demonstrates and which structural finding would strengthen the paper.
